Ladybird scales a selected face with size-adjust, including its glyphs
and metrics. Computed font-size stays unchanged, and font-size-adjust
overrides the descriptor. Automatic optical sizing follows the scaled
size, while an explicit opsz value stays unchanged.

Blink applies the descriptor in CSSFontFace::GetFontData(), through
FontDescription::SizeAdjustedFontDescription(). That helper skips the
scale when font-size-adjust is active. WebKit makes the same choice in
FontDescription::adjustedSizeForFontFace(), used by both downloaded and
local sources. Gecko applies the scale in gfxFont::GetAdjustedSize(),
with metric initialization overriding it for font-size-adjust. Its
function gfxFontEntry::GetVariationsForStyle() scales automatic optical
size while preserving explicit variation settings.

Ladybird invalidates selected fonts when FontFace.sizeAdjust changes, as
WebKit does through CSSFontFace::setSizeAdjust() and Gecko does through
FontFaceImpl::SetSizeAdjust() and DescriptorUpdated(). Blink’s
FontFace::setSizeAdjust() only sets the descriptor: Chrome keeps loaded
text at its earlier size after that setter. Ladybird retains its CSS-
connected descriptor reflection and invalidation behavior instead.

Ladybird resolves worker calculations using initial font metrics and a
zero-sized viewport. Blink uses MediaValuesCached defaults through its
FontFace::EnsureLengthResolver(): The em size is 16px and the viewport
is empty. Chrome renders Ahem with a 16-fold scale for a percentage
calculated from em or rem, and zero for vw, vh, or cqw. Ladybird matches
those resolved values, while keeping its computed serialization.

WebKit converts size-adjust in CSSFontFace::setSizeAdjust(), using the
deprecatedToStyleFromCSSValue() helper. Its calculation path calls
UnevaluatedCalcBase::evaluateDeprecated() without a length-conversion
context. Gecko uses NonNegativePercentage::compute() through function
Servo_FontFaceRule_GetSizeAdjust(), accepting only values resolvable at
parse time. Ladybird follows Blink for calculations needing a context.
